---
// The sign-in icon in the header, added by the colleague on 2026-09-25 (commit 35e8f80).
//
// Rewritten the same day with the browser-side sign-in. What changed and why:
// (Reworded 2026-09-26 for the move to Clerk, CLERK.md step 6: the first two items named the
// previous auth provider, which CLERK.md section 0 orders out of this branch. The design stands.)
//
// - The link goes to the sign-in page, and to the member's page once a session exists. It read
//   "/login" before, a route that never existed, so the icon led to a 404.
// - The script reads only the small flag the auth pages keep in localStorage
//   (src/scripts/auth-flag.ts) and never imports the auth library: this component is on every
//   page through Header.astro, and Clerk weighs about 720 KB gzip with React (measured 2026-09-26, see package.json) against about 70 KB of JavaScript
//   on the whole rest of the site. The flag is a hint for the icon; Clerk decides who is signed in.
// - The markup is a link and nothing else. The earlier version wrapped the <a> in a <button>, which
//   HTML does not allow, declared Props (href, className) that nothing read, and gave the SVG a
//   namespace that is not the SVG namespace; all three are gone.
// - The submit handler that used to end this file bound to a form on another page and could never
//   run; it lives in src/pages/auth/signin.astro now, next to its form.
//
// The icon used to be hidden on the home page, the colleague's choice (her note below describes the
// check), with no reason recorded. Changed the evening of 2026-09-25 at the owner's word: the home
// page is now the one page a guest sees - the carousel and a header of Home, the theme switch and
// this icon (AUTH.md section 10) - so the icon is the way in and shows there too. The check went
// with the condition it served; her note stays, as CLAUDE.md asks of existing comments.
import { site } from "../config";

// Проверяем, является ли текущая страница главной
// (The two lines that followed this note, reading Astro.url.pathname and computing isHomePage,
// were removed on the evening of 2026-09-25; see the paragraph above. The note is kept as it was.)
---

<div class="flex flex-1 justify-end">
  <a
    id="auth-link"
    href={site.auth.signIn}
    data-account-href={site.auth.account}
    class="ml-auto flex items-center justify-center gap-7 self-center p-2 text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:text-blue-600"
    aria-label="Войти на сайт"
    title="Войти на сайт"
  >
    <svg
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      fill="none"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      stroke-width="1.5"
      stroke="currentColor"
      class="h-6 w-6"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      <path
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        d="M15.75 9V5.25A2.25 2.25 0 0013.5 3h-6a2.25 2.25 0 00-2.25 2.25v13.5A2.25 2.25 0 007.5 21h6a2.25 2.25 0 002.25-2.25V15M12 9l-3 3m0 0l3 3m-3-3h12.75"
      ></path>
    </svg>
  </a>
</div>

<script>
  // Top level of the template, never inside a `{cond && (...)}` expression (the link sat in one
  // until the evening of 2026-09-25): a bundled script inside such a block is not hoisted at all
  // (CLAUDE.md, measured 2026-09-22). The script decides for itself whether there is a link to
  // update.
  import { readAuthFlag } from "../scripts/auth-flag";

  // Changed 2026-09-26 (CLERK.md step 2): the member's page is site.auth.account now, and the data
  // attribute is data-account-href to match; it was data-dashboard-href.
  const link = document.getElementById("auth-link");
  if (link instanceof HTMLAnchorElement && readAuthFlag()) {
    const account = link.dataset.accountHref;
    if (account !== undefined) link.href = account;
    link.setAttribute("aria-label", "Личный кабинет");
    link.title = "Личный кабинет";
  }
</script>
